 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Sessions use a dictionary in the web app's process. The shared store is
+[`sessions` in `larder/session_store.py`](../../larder/session_store.py). This removes the Postgres session query
+from each request, as requested by the volunteers to make the app faster; the performance improvement has not been
+measured.
 
-## Shaped by
+## Known limits
 
-- [Keep sessions in the database](../adrs/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)
+- Restarting or deploying the web app clears its sessions; members must log in again. Existing Postgres sessions
+  are not migrated, so switching stores also requires members to log in again.
+- Processes do not share sessions. In 2023, requests alternating between two servers logged members out, and deploys
+  logged everyone out; volunteers stopped deploying during opening hours. Use one web process, or route each member
+  consistently to one process, to avoid losing their session between requests. Routing does not preserve sessions
+  across restarts.
+- Stored sessions remain in memory until the process exits. The store does not enforce the lifetime above or remove
+  expired entries; callers must enforce expiry. Restarting releases the memory but also clears active sessions.
